## uic-measure: measure_box (MOD-04), the errors of the Measurements box

uic-measure-empty = Type a value, then press Enter.
uic-measure-not-a-value = “{ $text }” is not a number, a length or an angle.
uic-measure-not-accepted = This tool does not take “{ $kind }” now. It takes: { $accepted }.
uic-measure-too-many-values = Type one or two values, separated by { $separator }
uic-measure-bad-point = A point needs three values, for example { $example }
uic-measure-bad-brackets = A point starts with [ and ends with ] (absolute), or starts with < and ends with > (relative).
uic-measure-copies-zero = The number of copies must be 1 or more.
uic-measure-copies-large = At most { $max } copies.
uic-measure-divide-small = Divide into 2 parts or more.
uic-measure-divide-large = At most { $max } parts.
uic-measure-sides-range = The number of sides is from { $min } to { $max }.
uic-measure-negative = This value cannot be negative.
uic-measure-too-large = The value is too large.
uic-measure-kind-length = a length
uic-measure-kind-triple = three values
uic-measure-kind-factor = a scale factor
uic-measure-kind-pair = two values
uic-measure-kind-angle = an angle
uic-measure-kind-count = a number of copies
uic-measure-kind-divide = a division
uic-measure-kind-sides = a number of sides
uic-measure-kind-radius = a radius
uic-measure-kind-point-abs = an absolute point
uic-measure-kind-point-rel = a relative point
uic-measure-kind-none = no typed value
uic-measure-ambiguous-comma = “{ $text }” could be a decimal comma or a group of thousands. Write 1.5 for a decimal, or the number without the comma.
